 Stability\\\\LoopProbe 1440 704 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName LP2\r\nSYMBOL npn 1488 656 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q7\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3904\r\nSYMBOL npn 1808 656 M0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q6\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3904\r\nSYMBOL res 1632 736 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RT2\r\nSYMATTR Value 4.3k\r\nSYMBOL pnp 1808 624 R180\r\nSYMATTR InstName Q8\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N3906\r\nSYMBOL voltage 1856 688 R0\r\nWINDOW 0 24 16 Left 2\r\nWINDOW 3 24 96 Left 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName Vcm\r\nSYMATTR Value 0\r\nTEXT -64 880 Left 2 ;A differential pair (Q1, Q2) with PNP current-source loads (Q3, Q4); R2/R1 set the gain to -10 on each side. The loads take the common mode:\\nRcp and Rcn sense it (cm), Q6/Q7 compare it with Vcm and Q8 moves the bases of Q3 and Q4 (CMFB). LP1 (Stability > DiffLoopProbe) is in series\\nin the differential output, between the collectors (op, on) and the outputs (outp, outn): two ideal baluns separate the modes and the .stb picks one (dm or cm).\\nIn DM cm stays still and only the R2/R1 loop is left: one pole at the outputs, about 90° of margin.\r\nTEXT -64 1008 Left 2 ;.stb LP1 dm dec 50 1k 10g\r\n",
